Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.140
Speaker 1: Donald Trump has been looking for a&nbsp;
new defense lawyer even as late as this morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:14.760
just hours before today's arrest, booking and&nbsp;
arraignment. This is unbelievable stuff. Report&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:21.180
from The Washington Post. Trump Scrambles to Find&nbsp;
Lawyer before first federal court appearance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.400
What is happening? Donald Trump spent the day&nbsp;
before his historic appearance in federal court&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:33.300
scrambling to find a qualified Florida lawyer&nbsp;
willing to join his defense team as he faces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.340
the Justice Department's first prosecution of a&nbsp;
former president. This is yesterday after touching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:44.100
down in Miami Monday. Trump spent the afternoon&nbsp;
interviewing prospective lawyers and meeting with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.480
his legal team, along with other top advisers,&nbsp;
to discuss the case in which, as you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.640
he's accused of mishandling classified documents,&nbsp;
obstruction, etc.. Several prominent Florida&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:59.520
attorneys declined to take Trump on as a client&nbsp;
after two of the key lawyers handling the document&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.380
matter. Jim Trusty and John Rowley resigned&nbsp;
last week. A Trump adviser said late Monday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:09.360
Trump would be joined in court by Todd Blanch, an&nbsp;
attorney handling his case in New York, as well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:15.000
as veteran Florida litigator Christopher Case. On&nbsp;
the Truth Central platform, Trump said last week&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.760
Blanch would lead his defense team along with a&nbsp;
firm to be named later. This is not good. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.100
very much not good for Trump. The article goes on&nbsp;
to say Trust in Rowley's departure was sudden and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.900
unexpected, leaving Trump jockeying to identify&nbsp;
a lawyer ahead of today's appearance in federal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:35.940
court, where rules require practicing attorneys&nbsp;
to be members in good standing of the Florida bar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:42.180
or be sponsored by one before appearing case led&nbsp;
the search for a lawyer and cast a seemingly wide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:48.300
net. He declined to comment. The 11th hour flurry&nbsp;
to hire a seasoned trial attorney was a familiar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:53.160
dance for Trump, who has had difficulty hiring&nbsp;
and keeping lawyers over the course of federal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.120
and state investigations. Disagreements&nbsp;
over legal strategy hindered the search&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:03.360
for new defense attorneys. This is wild, wild&nbsp;
stuff. This is unbelievable. In a normal world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:09.000
attorneys would be qualified. Attorneys&nbsp;
would be falling all over themselves to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.880
defend a former president in an unprecedented&nbsp;
situation. But they are probably becoming aware&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:20.700
that when you tell Trump uncomfortable truths&nbsp;
like the indictment is strong or mistakes have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:26.580
been made up until now and we are now digging&nbsp;
out, or you might have to plea in some way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.880
Trump probably loses his mind. It's unclear&nbsp;
whether these lawyers would even be able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:38.820
get paid. So in a sense, in a situation where&nbsp;
lawyers should be desperate to work with Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.040
it's fascinating that there are even&nbsp;
lawyers still willing to represent Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:49.560
and it's probably a small subset of people&nbsp;
who are smart enough to pass the bar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:58.500
but not clever enough to realize that working with&nbsp;
Trump in this capacity is an impossibility because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:03.660
of the difficulties in both collecting payment and&nbsp;
getting Trump to actually do what you suggest that&nbsp;&nbsp;

